          'Present or past participle? Ask: does the noun itself do something, and at the same time? → present participle: der prüfende Mitarbeiter (= the employee who checks). Is something done to the noun, or has it already happened? → past participle: die geprüfte Rechnung (= the invoice that was checked). This is how a relative clause becomes a participial attribute: der Kollege, der anruft → der anrufende Kollege; der Kollege, der angerufen wurde → der angerufene Kollege.',
